# nr-exthost-pdf-font-object

Nothing in a hot file has to change for this task: it adds code to the three font files of mixdog-pdf that the fonts
task left empty, and one integration test. mixdog-pdf is already a workspace member; no dependency edge is new
(tests/fonts_twin.rs uses serde_json and mixdog-testkit, which the crate's dev-dependencies already have). No protocol
row, no SERVICE_PENDING name, no module line in lib.rs (`fonts` is declared).

One stale comment for whoever next edits native/core/crates/mixdog-pdf/src/fonts/mod.rs (owned by the fontdata task,
not touched here): its doc comment says `font`, `to_unicode` and `widths` are placeholders. They are filled now:

    //! The standard fonts and font dictionaries. `data` holds the tables and small functions ported from pdf.js; `font`
    //! (the font object and its loader), `to_unicode` (the character to text maps) and `widths` read a font dictionary.

What the text-content task (nr-exthost-pdf-textcontent) consumes, all in `mixdog_pdf::fonts`:

- `font::FontLoader::new(doc_id, ignore_errors)`: one per document (`doc_id` is pdf.js's document id, `d0`: the loaded
  names are `g_<doc_id>_f<n>`); `load_font(xref, font_name, font, resources, &LoadContext)` is `loadFont`. It returns
  an `Arc<TranslatedFont>` (`loaded_name`, `font()`, `chars_to_glyphs(bytes)`); an `ErrorFont` has no glyphs.
- `font::Font`: `vertical`, `ascent`, `descent`, `fallback_name`, `font_matrix`, `bbox`, `is_char_bbox`, `is_type3_font`,
  `missing_file`, `space_width()`; `font::Glyph`: `unicode` (UTF-16), `width`, `vmetric`, `is_space`, `category()`.
- `font::LoadContext { type3_font_refs, parsing_type3_font, type3 }`; the reader implements `font::Type3CharProcs`
  (the first operator of a Type 3 glyph description and the bounds of the paths it draws) so a Type 3 font gets the
  bounding box of its glyphs (`isCharBBox`); `font::NoType3Scan` reads nothing.
